./debate/steps/step-003/PROMPT_R1.md:380:claim: Both declared WINs rest on comparator C-indices that disagree with the local pipeline in one direction only. Julius reports SAFEHEART C=0.628 and FH-Risk-Score C=0.651 in UK Biobank; the local pipeline gets 0.6944 and 0.6740. Substituting the local values turns SAFEHEART 10-year from +0.079 [0.033,0.123] WIN to +0.013 TIE, and FH-RS from +0.052 [0.001,0.104] WIN to +0.030 TIE. Montreal, the only comparator needing neither Lp(a) nor LDL-C bands, reproduces to 0.003. The asymmetry is not random.
