91-This is a multicenter and multinational prospective cohort study. 
92-Subjects included in the present study were drawn from 5 pro-
93-spective registries of patients with FH: the Montreal Clinical 
94-Research Institute FH cohort (n=482), the FH registry from 
95-British Columbia (n=335), the UK Biobank (n=499), the Robarts 
96-Research Institute in Ontario (n=100), and the REFERCHOL 
97-FH registry from France (n=2465). Detailed description of 
98:these cohorts is available in Methods19 in the Data Supplement. 
99-All subjects had at least a probable diagnosis of FH accord-
100:ing to the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria (≥6 points), while 
101-the majority (74%) had definite FH with a positive molecular 
102-diagnosis. Subjects included in this study had no prior history 
103-of ASCVD. Subjects with a diagnosis of homozygous FH, those 
104-treated with LDL apheresis, and subjects under 18 years or 
105-over 65 years of age at baseline were excluded. Cardiovascular 
106:end points and data concerning the ASCVD predictors were 
107-collected by the treating physician during the patient’s clinical 
108-visits independently of the analysis of the data. Cardiovascular 
109:end points were individually validated using data from the clini-
110-cal chart, including data from emergency room visits, cardiology 
111-consultations, and testing (stress test, sestamibi scan, coronary 
112-angiography etc). Active smoking status was defined as current 
113-smoking, whereas ever smoking status was established for past, 
114-occasional, or current smokers. Statin intensity was considered 
115-low if the expected percent reduction in LDL-C according to 
